Description: CVE-2026-85730 - fix infinite loop (DoS) in skipUntil()
 In skipUntil(), the scanner looks for a separator while skipping inline
 comments. When a '#' is encountered it advances the cursor to the next
 newline via indexOfNewline(). If the comment has no trailing newline,
 indexOfNewline() returns -1; the subsequent loop increment (i++) then resets
 the cursor to 0 and the scan restarts from the beginning of the string,
 producing an unbounded loop that never terminates. A crafted TOML document
 such as "a = [0#" reaches this path and hangs the parser.
 .
 Add a guard so that a negative index (end of input with no newline) breaks
 out of the loop, allowing the existing "cannot find end of structure"
 TomlError to be raised instead of looping forever.
 .
 The published npm package ships only the compiled output, so the fix is
 applied to the emitted ESM module (dist/util.js) and the bundled CommonJS
 entry point (dist/index.cjs), which both contain a copy of skipUntil().
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/squirrelchat/smol-toml/commit/30f5c367d946b695f379b5d4f0946b2f0a0a8c2f
